<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="getting-started-step-by-step-index">
  <title>Step by step</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>This series builds upon the <url href="https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/getting_started/introduction/key_concepts_overview.html#doc-key-concepts-overview">Introduction to Godot</url> and will get you started with the editor and the
            engine. You will learn more about nodes and scenes, code your first classes with
            GDScript, use signals to make nodes communicate with one another, and more.</p>
    <p>The following lessons are here to prepare you for <xref ref="getting-started-first-2d-game-index-your-first-2d-game" text="custom">Your first 2D game</xref>, a
            step-by-step tutorial where you will code a game from scratch. By the end of it,
            you will have the necessary foundations to explore more features in other
            sections. We also included links to pages that cover a given topic in-depth
            where appropriate.</p>
     </introduction>
  <xi:include href="nodes_and_scenes.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="instancing.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="scripting_first_script.ptx" />
